# SETAR 1.5: exercise the package's own LR confidence-profile graph.
# Its official example uses a remotely fetched lynx dataset; avoid that dependency.
# Box-Jenkins monthly passenger growth provides a genuine local time series.
# No linearity bootstrap: the native threshold confidence plot is unconditional.
open bjg.gdt --quiet
series y = diff(lg)
set seed 320102
list fitted = SETAR(y, 2, 2, null, 0, 0)
# SETAR() itself issues gnuplot ... --single-yaxis with a dynamic yrange.
